course: dictionary
lesson: 16065
title: Words about volcanoes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something came from or how it was made. Volcanically is one of these. It means because of volcanoes, or in the way a volcano works. «The island was formed volcanically» means volcanoes helped to build the island.
explain: Look for the clue inside the word. Volcanic is about volcanoes, and the ending -ally turns it into an adverb, a word that tells how something happens. So volcanically tells you how something is done or what it is caused by.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «Hawaii is volcanically active, and new land is still forming there.» The words active and forming are clues. They link to volcanoes, so volcanically must be about volcanoes.
fact: Volcanically means because of volcanoes or in the way of a volcano.
fact: «Volcanically active» describes a place where volcanoes still erupt or where hot springs rise from the ground.
fact: Iceland, Hawaii, Japan and the North Island of New Zealand are all volcanically active places.
fact: Islands and rocks can be formed volcanically, which means volcanoes helped to make them.
fact: Volcanically is built from volcanic and -ally, so it describes how something happens.
exercise: «Iceland is volcanically active, with hot springs and eruptions.» What does volcanically mean here? | Under the sea only | Because of rain and wind | *Because of volcanoes | Very cold and icy
exercise: «Hawaii is volcanically active.» What does volcanically active suggest? | *Eruptions and hot springs can still happen there | There are no hills or mountains at all | People have never lived there | The place is always covered in snow
exercise: Mia reads «The island was formed volcanically» and says volcanically means bumpy. What does it really mean? | Very old and ancient | Bumpy and uneven | *Because of volcanoes, so volcanoes helped to make the island | Under the water only
test: «New Zealand's North Island is volcanically active.» What does this tell you? | The island is covered in ice all year | *Volcanoes there are still active | There are no volcanoes there at all | The island was painted by an artist
test: Which place is volcanically active? | A desert with no hills | *Japan | A school playground | A flat field with no rocks
exam: Explain what «volcanically formed» means in your own words. | Painted by children in a art lesson | Found only in shops | Made of ice and snow | *Made with help from volcanoes
